Z||000000||fiero56||03-24-2001||11:44 AM||||I ran searches last night, found the model year, wrote everythgin down, and decided to check out these Cavalier rotors compared to Fiero rotors myself.<P>Walking through the door armed with a dial caliper, I find out the Cavalier rotors are thinner, and have a larger diameter than stock '88 Fiero rotors. Anyone have factory specs on what both rotors' sizes are supposed to be new? I'm not talking about when they are considered trash, but what is the diameter and width of them out of the box? <BR>I'm not impressed, not going to be doing the Cavalier thing with my '88, I'll pay the $100/pair for the right thing, rather than $30/pair for what "should" work. I guinea pigged the ATF thing, not doing rotors too.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric||03-24-2001||11:49 AM||||I probably wouldn't do it again, because the inner surface grinds the dust shield.  It made a ton of noise for about two weeks.  Other than that, they work fine even if they are a little different.||||reg||1
